    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bardolph was originally laid out on August 3, 1852 by William H. and was first called “Randolph” before being renamed to avoid duplication.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitforgottonia.com/village-of-bardolph/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town grew rapidly after a public auction of about 50 lots in June 1868, when Hendricks bought half interest and sold lots.",
